_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I89a5f6ba6f9233abf4651a0b66360548c92629c3" commit="9431cc3b26f6ec480fef569ebc7cc727f12177c4" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: rt5645: Prevent the weird sound of the headphone while rebooting  The patch adds the codec reset setting in the shutdown function to prevent the weird sound of the headphone happened by rebooting.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40164,chrome-os-partner:46042 TEST=test audio on celes  Signed-off-by: Oder Chiou &lt;oder_chiou@realtek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit a2c026cfec3fb84375785dd2d6ec80bd60c5120e) Signed-off-by: Wonjoon Lee &lt;woojoo.lee@samsung.com&gt;  Change-Id: I89a5f6ba6f9233abf4651a0b66360548c92629c3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304465 Commit-Ready: Wonjoon Lee &lt;woojoo.lee@samsung.com&gt; Tested-by: Wonjoon Lee &lt;woojoo.lee@samsung.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304465" owner_email="woojoo.lee@samsung.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/65/304465/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I3413c5cb81eeb8836fe15030b9cfcc29e6ac738e" commit="b28be51bf90af908e6998628a624e01f01e9b639" commit_message="iio:light:ap3223 Added events support to ap3223 driver  This adds the events support to the ap3223 ambient light and proximity sensor driver. A chrdev (/dev/iio:device0) is created which can be used by the applications to monitor the events from the driver. This also adds interface to enable and disable the events (in sysfs).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46132 BRANCH=None TEST=As usual, the following sysfs interfaces can be used to read the raw values /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device0/in_illuminance_raw /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device0/in_proximity_raw The following file can be used to [en/dis]able the events /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device0/events/in_proximity_thresh_either_en by writing either a 1(enable) or 0(disable). One can write an app to read the chardev by following the sample app at drivers/staging/iio/Documentation/iio_event_monitor.c found in 3.14 version of the kernel. I have tested all the interfaces described above.  Change-Id: I3413c5cb81eeb8836fe15030b9cfcc29e6ac738e Signed-off-by: Suresh Rajashekara &lt;sureshraj@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303975 Commit-Ready: Suresh Rajashekara &lt;sureshraj@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Suresh Rajashekara &lt;sureshraj@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bryan Freed &lt;bfreed@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303975" owner_email="sureshraj@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/75/303975/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5c65a56f4a1a4970cf16c31ac49ae73565e65b2d" commit="e8f23ec5e36f849fbda16f8be1b31fa1a08eb0c8" commit_message="vboot: draw screens using cbgfx  This change makes vboot_draw_screen draw vboot screens using cbgfx APIs.  BUG=chromium:502066 BRANCH=tot TEST=Tested on Samus, Jerry, Smaug  Change-Id: I5c65a56f4a1a4970cf16c31ac49ae73565e65b2d Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303074 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303074" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="26" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/74/303074/26" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I64cae681c43a6162c406ed1172852ae7108edecf" commit="7815c216ba398f4be5024def819803b59a7ba3fa" commit_message="CHROMIUM: dmc: Add dummy rockchip_dmc_enable/disable for CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP=n  rockchip platform will disable dmc when detect usb speaker plug in usb sound, to pervent build issue add dummy rockchip_enable/disable function when CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP=n  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43539 TEST=None  Change-Id: I64cae681c43a6162c406ed1172852ae7108edecf Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304510 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304510" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/10/304510/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic2bdb35cff17cf8c1789db78c7166a404610827b" commit="9a2b3f906080bf9972aad82421e8dacd3d0b54e0" commit_message="[autotest] Make explicit that lock_reason of AbstractHostModel can be NULL.  lock_reason of AbstractHostModel didn't specify null property explicitly. The effect of it is MySQL has NULL property for lock_reason column, but Sqlite doesn't have NULL property for the column. simple_heartbeat_client.py uses in-memory sqlite, and it produces error like below.  django.db.utils.IntegrityError: NOT NULL constraint failed: afe_hosts.lock_reason  This means a host entry got from prod database has NULL lock_reason, and it violates integrity for sqlite DB. We should make it explicit that lock_reason column can be NULL.  BUG=None TEST=Run simple_heartbeat_client.py in local machine.  Change-Id: Ic2bdb35cff17cf8c1789db78c7166a404610827b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304577 Commit-Ready: Mungyung Ryu &lt;mkryu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Mungyung Ryu &lt;mkryu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthew Sartori &lt;msartori@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304577" owner_email="mkryu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/77/304577/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If2690af965c6be7254f1c49a73cfae7161569ba8" commit="6e207389f2d84ffbfad25527ecdb06cabd4a2901" commit_message="GCC: Upgrade GCC (merge from google/4_9 branch + cherry-picks)  Backport r226487 from GCC FSF mainline:    r226487 | rguenth | 2015-08-03 00:13:36 -0700 (Mon, 03 Aug 2015)    2015-08-03  Richard Biener  &lt;rguenther@suse.de&gt;   PR tree-optimization/66917  * tree-vectorizer.h (struct dataref_aux): Add base_element_aligned  field.  (DR_VECT_AUX): New macro.  (set_dr_misalignment): Adjust.  (dr_misalignment): Likewise.  * tree-vect-data-refs.c (vect_compute_data_ref_alignment):  Compute whether the base is at least element aligned.  * tree-vect-stmts.c (ensure_base_align): Adjust.  (vectorizable_store): If the base is not element aligned  preserve alignment of the original access if misalignment is unknown.  (vectorizable_load): Likewise.  ------------------------------------------------------------------------  Backport r223811 from gcc-5-branch:      PR libstdc++/66017     * include/bits/stl_tree.h (_Rb_tree_node): Use __aligned_membuf.     (_Rb_tree_iterator, _Rb_tree_const_iterator): Support construction     from _Base_ptr.     (_Rb_tree_const_iterator::_M_const_cast): Remove static_cast.     (_Rb_tree::begin, _Rb_tree::end): Remove static_cast.     * include/ext/aligned_buffer.h (__aligned_membuf): New type using     alignment of _Tp as a member subobject, not as a complete object.     * python/libstdcxx/v6/printers.py (StdRbtreeIteratorPrinter): Lookup     _Link_type manually as it might not be in the debug info.  ------------------------------------------------------------------------  Merge google/gcc-4_9 (220271:227810] into google/gcc-4_9-mobile branch.  BUG=chromium:532101     chromium:530369 TEST=Done GCC bootstrapping &amp; regression test, plus building ChromeOS      images &amp; testing them on various boards, for x86, x86_64 and arm;      also built arm64-generic ChromeOS image.  Change-Id: If2690af965c6be7254f1c49a73cfae7161569ba8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302402 Commit-Ready: Luis Lozano &lt;llozano@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Luis Lozano &lt;llozano@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Han Shen &lt;shenhan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302402" owner_email="cmtice@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/gcc" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/gcc" ref="refs/changes/02/302402/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7528.0.0-rc5"/></manifest>